# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Without this file the context is ~19 GB — `target/` alone is the whole local
# build cache — and every byte is uploaded to the builder before the first
# instruction runs. On a PaaS that is a failed or absurdly slow deploy, and the
# cache is worthless anyway: the image compiles from scratch inside the builder
# stage against its own pinned toolchain.

# Build output — the single largest offender.
target/
**/target/

# Version-control metadata. The build needs the sources, not the history.
.git/
.github/

# Local state that must never be baked into an image: a key file here would be
# readable by anyone who pulls the image.
.env
*.env
!keys.env.example
!.env.example
.huntsman/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Editor / OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Android/Termux-only assets that have no role in a container build.
.cargo/config.toml

# Documentation and CI config: not needed to compile, and excluding them keeps
# an unrelated doc edit from invalidating the Docker layer cache.
docs/
scripts/
fuzz/

# NOT excluded, deliberately:
#   benches/  — Cargo.toml declares [[bench]] targets whose paths default to
#               benches/<name>.rs. Excluding them risks a manifest resolution
#               error for no meaningful context saving.
#   build.rs  — required; it generates the source manifest from src/.
#   README.md — tiny, and referenced by packaging metadata.
